<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!-- SpotBugs project decisions: a rule, or a rule in part of the code, that the team has decided not
     to enforce. One Match per decision, with a comment giving the reason, for example:

       <!- - JPA entities share associations by design (reason ...) - ->
       <Match><Package name="~team\.projectpulse\..*"/><Bug pattern="EI_EXPOSE_REP"/></Match>

     Unlike the baseline, this file may grow, but every entry is a reviewed decision. -->
<FindBugsFilter>
  <!-- D1, EI_EXPOSE_REP and EI_EXPOSE_REP2: not enforced (decided 2026-11-13, 219 findings triaged).
       Every finding is one of three kinds, none of which is a defect here:
       (1) JPA entities returning or storing their associations and collections. Hibernate must hand out the
           managed instance it tracks; a defensive copy in a getter or setter breaks dirty checking,
           orphanRemoval, and lazy loading.
       (2) Spring beans storing constructor-injected collaborators. Those are shared singletons by design.
       (3) DTO records and report POJOs holding Lists. They are built in one service method and handed
           straight to Jackson, and nothing mutates them afterwards.
       Project Pulse is one deployable with no untrusted code in the same JVM, so exposing internal
       representation is not a security boundary. SpotBugs filters cannot match by annotation, so narrowing
       to entities and beans would mean a hand-kept class list that silently goes stale. -->
  <Match><Bug pattern="EI_EXPOSE_REP,EI_EXPOSE_REP2"/></Match>
</FindBugsFilter>
